Description: Calculates nitrogen, phosphorus (P2O5) and potassium (K2O) fertilization
    requirements with the crop nutrient balance and the simplified
    standard-dose methods of the Emilia-Romagna Integrated Production
    Guidelines (Disciplinari di Produzione Integrata, DPI 2026), reproducing
    the regional reference tool Fert_Office (v1.26). The nitrogen balance
    accounts for crop demand, soil supply, leaching, immobilization, previous
    crop residues, current and previous organic fertilization and natural
    deposition. The package also provides soil texture and chemistry
    classifiers, maximum allowed nitrogen doses, Olsen P and exchangeable K
    availability classes, an organic plus mineral distribution plan with the
    Nitrates Directive check, end-of-cycle soil P and K estimation, farm and
    pixel-level spatial balances, a vegetation index engine for Sentinel-2 and
    drone imagery, Gaussian-process retrieval of canopy traits from Sentinel-2
    Level-2A data, the Nitrogen Nutrition Index (Lemaire and Gastal, 1997),
    and variable-rate prescriptions (calibration ramp, Holland and Schepers
    sufficiency index, nutrition-index zones) constrained to the balance dose,
    with optional economic optimisation through 'Rquefts' and export to
    machine formats. All coefficient tables are editable R objects, so the
    balance can be re-parameterized for other guidelines.
